  "summary": "Remote-controlled shell/PTY over vendor WebSocket in @ai-support-agent/cli",
  "details": "The package ships a daemon that maintains an outbound WebSocket/AppSync connection to api.ai-support-agent.com and executes commands received over that channel on the installer's host. In dist/vscode/vscode-server.js and related handlers, an `execute_command` message dispatches its payload string to `executeShellCommand`, and a terminal `stdin` message has its base64-decoded bytes written directly into a `node-pty` session spawned on the user's `$SHELL`. The daemon also proxies a code-server instance and supports an `ssh_exec` operation that runs arbitrary commands using SSH credentials fetched from the vendor API. Any party that controls or compromises the vendor side of the connection (or a tenant token) obtains interactive, full-host command execution as the user running the daemon. The package additionally installs itself as a persistent OS service on macOS and Linux with PATH modifications (dist/cli/service/darwin-service.js, dist/cli/service/linux-service.js), which keeps the remote-control channel live across reboots.",
